    fn::llhttp_set_lenient_transfer_encoding
    fn::llhttp_set_lenient_version

    The parser's API api.c gives. Thirteen items are a field's read or
    write, or a map's text, that llhttp.rs already gives: the getters,
    llhttp_set_error_reason and the three X-macro generators are ported as
    ParserRef's accessors and the maps' constant_name / map_string, which
    carry their Replaces anchors. Native in api.rs: ParserMut::execute,
    pause, resume, resume_after_upgrade, the ten set_lenient_* setters and
    ParserRef::debug_trace (llhttp__debug, compiled but uncalled on this
    build), which writes through glibc-bindings' locked fprintf on C's
    stderr, the crustify-campaign route; the sign-extended high byte of
    C's %02x is not carried over.

    The six functions C outside api.c calls (llhttp_execute,
    llhttp_get_error_pos, llhttp_get_error_reason, llhttp_pause,
    llhttp_resume, llhttp_resume_after_upgrade) are exported under the new
    export feature ffi-export-deps-llhttp-api-c, off, each checked against
    its raw binding. The raw bindings gain llhttp_lenient_flags and fifteen
    functions; the 25 functions' pointer findings are submitted to the
    ownership store. Four unit_priv, thirteen unit_pub, two ub_safe, four
    equiv tests and three doctests. Proposals:
    port-onto-an-existing-accessor (porting-symbols) and
    std-macro-expansions-outside-regions (conventions, ffimap).

    Co-Authored-By: crustify <crustify@berkeley.edu>

